The vendored module aimara/rob/_voice_identity.py is copied without functional
changes from Eurecat/EutSpeechAudioProcessing:

  speech_recognition/speech_recognition/voice_identity_manager.py
  commit fd89b8b537c17b7ccd103310039ddcf6faf7aa4e
  https://github.com/Eurecat/EutSpeechAudioProcessing

It is distributed under the upstream Apache License 2.0. See
EutSpeechAudioProcessing.LICENSE in this directory. Aimara uses the session-only
matcher; its optional MongoDB and fleet synchronization paths are not activated.

Sentence grouping and short-run smoothing in aimara/speaker_segmentation.py are
adapted from ASREngine in the same upstream commit:
  speech_recognition/speech_recognition/asr_engine.py

aimara/rob_native.py loads the original ASR, VAD, REDI, and identity engines
directly from a separately installed checkout at this same pinned commit. It
also compiles the unchanged _vad_callback and _on_eut_speaker_changed method
bodies from upstream DiarizationNode for replay without ROS transport. That
source remains covered by the upstream Apache License 2.0. The local replay
scheduler and read-only group export are AIMARA integration code.
